   "tz": "Atlantic/Canary",
   "intro": "The high crater floor of Las Cañadas around Mount Teide, an hour or so by road from the coastal resorts of Tenerife.",
   "facts": [
    "Teide National Park holds Starlight certification both as a tourist destination and as a reserve.",
    "The Teide Observatory, run by the Instituto de Astrofísica de Canarias, sits at about 2,390 m in the park.",
    "Canary Islands law has protected the sky over the observatories from light pollution since 1988.",
    "Low clouds usually form below a temperature inversion that sits well under the peaks, so the park can be clear when the coast is cloudy."
   ],
   "tip": "It is cold at night up here even in summer. Bring warm layers, and check the road and weather before you drive up.",
